<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>Barbatos.SecsGem.PerformanceTracking</PackageId>
    <TargetFrameworks>$(BarbatosTargetFrameworks)</TargetFrameworks>
    <RootNamespace>Barbatos.SecsGem.PerformanceTracking</RootNamespace>
    <PackageTags>secs;e116;ept;utilisation;oee;equipment;performance;fab300;stream14</PackageTags>
    <Description>Equipment performance tracking (SEMI E116) for .NET: a machine's modules, the three states E116 gives each of them - idle, executing, blocked - and where the time actually went. The distinction the standard exists for is the one between having nothing to do and being stopped by something, because those two have different owners; a task survives a block, so the time a job spends waiting is charged to that job as well as to the module. Every duration is measured through a TimeProvider from a monotonic timestamp, so an operator correcting the machine's clock cannot push a chamber's utilisation above one and a test needs no wall clock. E116 has no message set of its own: a module is an object, and its state and accounting reach a host through SECS-II stream 14 object services - read-only and with no actions, on purpose, since a host that could assign an EPT state could record a chamber as productive while it stood empty. Depends on Barbatos.SecsGem.Objects and Barbatos.SecsGem.Hsms, and not on GEM: the collection events E116 defines are raised as events for an application to publish through whatever reports it already has.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Barbatos.SecsGem.Core\Barbatos.SecsGem.Core.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Barbatos.SecsGem.Hsms\Barbatos.SecsGem.Hsms.csproj" />
    <!-- E116 is a state model and nothing else: every attribute a host reads comes through
         stream 14, so this is the one dependency that is not optional. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Barbatos.SecsGem.Objects\Barbatos.SecsGem.Objects.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
